{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4c9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a823-e600-7521-9ce0-62cc9653cb46"},"sequence":191,"recorded_at":1780531400000377,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a02c0fe6-9135-4b16-8f63-6f987d7b0b4a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a02c0fe6-9135-4b16-8f63-6f987d7b0b4a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a02c0fe6-9135-4b16-8f63-6f987d7b0b4a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a824-585a-7361-934c-05e89dc87a13"},"task_id":"01a0a824-585a-7361-934c-05e89dc87a13","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a824-585a-7361-934c-05e89dc87a13","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Documents/Codex/2026-09-15/new-chat-4/outputs/RunnerControl/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260916-97dhxd/TASK-260916-97dhxd_outcome.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-97dhxd — github-login-and-management-window — outcome\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (board `to-review` via handoff).\n4|\n5|## What shipped (uncommitted candidate in Story worktree)\n6|\n7|- `GitHubAuth` Relux module (actor services, HybridState/reducer/Flow, Module):\n8|  `GitHubAuth.swift`, `GitHubAuth+State.swift`, `GitHubAuth+State+Reducer.swift`,\n9|  `GitHubAuth+Flow.swift`, `GitHubAuth+Module.swift`, `GitHubAuth+Models.swift`.\n10|- Transport/security: `GitHubAppConfig.swift` (public client_id only, exact\n11|  missing binding, `auditNoSecrets`), `GitHubTransport.swift` (HTTP boundary,\n12|  DTOs, `RESTMapper`, `PATGuard`), `GitHubDeviceFlow.swift` (code/poll,\n13|  slow_down +5), `GitHubAPIClient.swift` (/user, installations, repos),\n14|  `GitHubTokenRefresh.swift` (serialized single-flight refresh),\n15|  `GitHubKeychainStore.swift` (Keychain + in-memory backend),\n16|  `GitHubRedaction.swift` (diagnostic scrub).\n17|- App: `ManagementWindowContainer.swift` + `ManagementWindowPage.swift` (+Props)\n18|  760×540 tabs (Runners/GitHub/General), `LaunchAtLoginModel.swift`,\n19|  `AppRegistry.swift` (both modules, 3s local / 30s GitHub loops),\n20|  `App.swift` (management window via reopen + notification, no new delegate),\n21|  `RunnerContainer/Page` + \"Раннеры и настройки…\" (menu intact).\n22|- Generator input only: `ios-app-manager.json` adds\n23|  `macos.info_plist.GitHubAppClientID: \"\"` (placeholder; coordinator provisions\n24|  real public client_id, then `ios-app-manager generate macos-app` converges\n25|  `Project.swift`). `Project.swift`/`Package.swift` untouched by hand.\n26|- `.spec/` materialized from approved-design with registration + removal in\n27|  scope: README, github-login-device-flow, management-window,\n28|  runner-registration, runner-removal, offline-local-control.\n29|\n30|Missing binding (exact, user-visible when unprovisioned):\n31|`Info.plist[GitHubAppClientID] (scaffold input ios-app-manager.json →\n32|macos.info_plist.GitHubAppClientID, coordinator-provisioned public client_id)`\n33|\n34|## AC coverage — 9 of 11 rows driven via committed tests\n35|\n36|| # | AC row | Named committed test(s) | Production call site |\n37||---|---|---|---|\n38|| 1 | App builds | BOUND (verified via build commands below, not a unit test) | `Scripts/build.sh` path: `tuist generate`, `xcodebuild -scheme RunnerControl`, `codesign --verify` |\n39|| 2 | Real login UI drives production services | `flowLoginSuccessDrivesProductionEffectsToConnected` (Flow path UI calls; UI binding manual, no UI tests per task) | `ManagementWindowContainer.beginLogin → action { GitHubAuth.Effect.beginLogin } → GitHubAuth.Flow.apply` |\n40|| 3 | Cancellation | `flowCancellationDestroysCodeAndStopsPoll`, `flowCancelWhileConnectedRestoresConnected` | `GitHubAuth.Flow.apply(.cancelLogin)` |\n41|| 4 | slow_down | `flowSlowDownIncreasesIntervalThenSucceeds`, `slowDownAddsFiveSeconds` | `GitHubDeviceFlow.pollOnce` + `nextInterval` via `Flow.apply(.beginLogin)` |\n42|| 5 | Expired code | `flowExpiredCodeFailsWithNewCode` | `GitHubDeviceFlow.pollOnce` via `Flow.apply(.beginLogin)` |\n43|| 6 | Refresh concurrency | `refreshSavesAtomicallyAndCoalescesConcurrentCallers` | `GitHubTokenRefresh.refresh` |\n44|| 7 | Logout | `flowLogoutClearsKeychainAndStopsSync` | `GitHubAuth.Flow.apply(.logout)` |\n45|| 8 | 401 | `apiClientMaps401And403`, `flow401DuringRefreshRequiresRelogin` | `GitHubAPIClient.fetchInstallations` + `Flow.apply(.refreshInstallations)` |\n46|| 9 | 403 | `apiClientMaps401And403`, `flow403DuringRefreshKeepsConnectedWithStaleError` | `GitHubAPIClient.fetchInstallations` + `Flow.apply(.refreshInstallations)` |\n47|| 10 | No PAT fallback | `patGuardRejectsClassicAndFineGrainedPAT`, `apiClientRefusesPATWithoutNetwork`, `devicePollRejectsPATShapedToken` | `GitHubAuth.PATGuard.validate/authorizationHeader` via `GitHubAPIClient`/`GitHubDeviceFlow` |\n48|| 11 | Existing menu functional | BOUND (Runners suite green incl. `reducerPreserves…`, `startIsIdempotent…`, `startWaits…`; menu UI wiring manual, no UI tests) | `RunnerContainer.change → Runners.Effect.setEnabled → Runners.Flow.apply` |\n49|\n50|## Validation (real exit codes)\n51|\n52|- `swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore` → exit 0, 45 tests passed.\n53|- Skill script `run-macos-package-tests.sh --package Packages/RunnerControlCore --output .temp/macos-tests` → exit 0, 45 passed, JUnit/logs under `.temp/macos-tests`.\n54|- `tuist generate --no-open` → exit 0.\n55|- `xcodebuild -workspace RunnerControl.xcworkspace -scheme RunnerControl -configuration Release -destination 'platform=macOS' … build` → BUILD SUCCEEDED (exit 0 via grep; full log exit 65 only on the pre-fix run, 0 after closure fix).\n56|- `codesign --verify --deep --strict .temp/products/RunnerControl.app` → exit 0; bundle `works.relux.runnercontrol`, version `1.1.1`.\n57|- `swiftlint lint` on new files → exit 0, 0 serious (warnings only; pre-existing files carry their own baseline warnings; `ManagementWindowPage` split to fix `type_body_length` error).\n58|- Not run: `RUN_LAUNCH_AGENT_INTEGRATION=1` launchd integration (touches host launchd; default suite skips it), UI tests (forbidden by task), release/notary (other Story).\n59|\n60|## Narrowing mutant evidence (gate stays, weakened to admit one member)\n61|\n62|| Mutant | Narrowing (what it admits) | Named test that fails | Result |\n63||---|---|---|---|\n64|| M1 PAT `ghp_` only | admits `github_pat_*` | `patGuardRejectsClassicAndFineGrainedPAT` | KILLED (exit 1, \"admitted PAT 'github_pat_abc123'\") |\n65|| M2 REST 403 disabled (`4030`) | 403 falls to generic network | `apiClientMaps401And403` | KILLED (exit 1, got `.network` not `.forbidden`) |\n66|| M3 `expired_token → pending` | expired loops as pending | `flowExpiredCodeFailsWithNewCode` | KILLED (exit 1, got `.retry` not `.newCode`) |\n67|| M4 slow_down no +5 | interval stays 5 | `flowSlowDownIncreasesIntervalThenSucceeds` | KILLED (exit 1, got `pollIntervalUpdated(5)` not 10) |\n68|| M5 `inFlight` disabled | concurrent refresh does 2× HTTP | `refreshSavesAtomicallyAndCoalescesConcurrentCallers` | KILLED (exit 1, `requests.count == 1` failed) |\n69|| M6 logout skips Keychain delete | token survives logout | `flowLogoutClearsKeychainAndStopsSync` | KILLED (exit 1, `load(...) == nil` failed) |\n70|| M7 audit `secret`-only | admits `private_key`/`token` keys | `auditRejectsEmbeddedSecrets` | KILLED (exit 1, admitted `AppPrivateKey`, `GitHubToken`, …) |\n71|| M8 redaction drops `device_code` | `dev789` leaks | `redactionScrubsExactSecretsAndJSONShapes` | KILLED (exit 1, `contains(\"dev789\")`) |\n72|| M9 cancel drops `pollTask.cancel` | relies on generation+nil only | — (survivor) | SURVIVED (exit 0). Bound: cancellation has triple redundancy (generation + Task.cancel + `deviceCode=nil`); dropping Task.cancel alone still stops via generation check. Test proves generation gate, not Task.cancel necessity. |\n73|| M9c cancel only when connected | login-phase cancel skips generation+cancel | — (survivor) | SURVIVED (exit 0). Bound: `deviceCode=nil` alone stops the sleep-phase loop via `guard let code`; test timing (cancel during sleep) does not isolate generation. |\n74|| M9d cancel always `loginCancelled` | connected-cancel disconnects | `flowCancelWhileConnectedRestoresConnected` | KILLED (exit 1, got `loginCancelled` not `connected`) |\n75|\n76|No source-text (grep) gates shipped; PAT/secret enforcement is behavioral\n77|(`PATGuard`, `auditNoSecrets`, `Redaction`), so the \"preserve token\" mutant\n78|clause is N/A. Delete-only mutants were not used as evidence.\n79|\n80|## Notes / bounds\n81|\n82|- Tokens/`device_code` never in `GitHubAuth.State`, logs, or `RuntimeLogger`\n83|  (type-only). Keychain account `<host>:<userID>:<clientID>`.\n84|- Offline/403/rate-limit keep local control; 401/revoked → relogin. Stale\n85|  `busy=false` (>60s) is labeled stale, never idle proof.\n86|- Enterprise hosts get host-scoped endpoints; App registration + Device Flow\n87|  support must be verified per server (concrete error, local works).\n88|- No `gh` credential import, no PAT UI, no client secret/private key fields.\n89|- Work left uncommitted in Story worktree for handoff snapshot (no producer commit).","final_result":true}}}
