{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c75f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a823-e600-7521-9ce0-62cc9653cb46"},"sequence":522,"recorded_at":1780531400001039,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a02c0fe6-9135-4b16-8f63-6f987d7b0b4a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a02c0fe6-9135-4b16-8f63-6f987d7b0b4a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a02c0fe6-9135-4b16-8f63-6f987d7b0b4a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a824-d5f3-71d0-a0b1-cb54122f23db"},"task_id":"01a0a824-d5f3-71d0-a0b1-cb54122f23db","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a824-d5f3-71d0-a0b1-cb54122f23db","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-9-1\",\n  \"command\": \"ls /Users/iv/Documents/Codex/2026-09-15/new-chat-4/work/skills/skill-ios-app-manager/references/ 2>&1\\ncat \\\"/Users/iv/Documents/Codex/2026-09-15/new-chat-4/work/skills/skill-ios-app-manager/references/native-macos.md\\\" 2>&1 | head -n 300\\necho \\\"===GENERATOR-HELP===\\\"\\n/Users/iv/Documents/Codex/2026-09-15/new-chat-4/work/ios-app-manager --help 2>&1 | head -n 100\",\n  \"description\": \"Read macOS generator docs and help\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"build-profiling-research.md\\ncli-reference.md\\ndsl-reference.md\\nlayout-hierarchy-diagnostics-research.md\\nnative-macos.md\\nphysical-ios-launch-log-workflow.md\\nprofile-diagnostics-architecture.md\\nruntime-error-diagnostics-research.md\\nruntime-profiles.md\\nruntime-profiles.schema.json\\nruntime-profiling-research.md\\ntree-httpclient.md\\ntree-ioc.md\\ntree-relux.md\\ntree-shared-modules.md\\ntree-tuist.md\\nworkflows.md\\n# Native macOS apps\\n\\n## Scaffold gap\\n\\nThe iOS init pipeline exposes iPhone/iPad destinations, iOS deployment settings and iOS-specific capability helpers. A native macOS menu-bar app needs macOS destinations, LSUIElement, explicit sandbox policy and hostless unit tests. Do not manually patch generated Project.swift to achieve this.\\n\\n## Owning plugin\\n\\n`ios-app-manager generate macos-app --config ios-app-manager.json` is a standalone scaffold plugin (no iOS init dependency). It orchestrates manifest, package, app-entry and unit-test subgenerators. It generates a native Tuist app, a `<AppName>Core` framework and a hostless `<AppName>CoreTests` target; no UI-test target. `min_target` means macOS version and must be 13.0 or newer. Set `macos: {menu_bar: true, sandbox: false, packages: [{url: \\\"https://example.com/package.git\\\", version: \\\"1.0.0\\\", product: \\\"Example\\\"}]}` with the normal identity/version fields. Disable sandbox only for apps that need host process/service control. Explicit package versions are pinned exactly and exposed to the Core framework. The app imports its Core facade. Store business logic in Core, platform UI in the app.\\n\\nRe-run this command to converge config-owned Project.swift and Workspace.swift. Source files are seeded only when absent, so handwritten code/tests survive regeneration. The separate Core Package.swift enables `swift test --package-path Packages/<AppName>Core` on macOS. Native Xcode packages and SwiftPM use the same configured exact versions. The package manifest is config-owned too. Do not mix the iOS `generate project-config` orchestration into this native scaffold; use `generate macos-app` for synchronization.\\n\\nGenerate with `tuist generate --no-open`, then build with `xcodebuild -workspace <AppName>.xcworkspace -scheme <AppName> -destination 'platform=macOS' build`. Sign using the configured DEVELOPMENT_TEAM; do not silently substitute another team. The generated app source is a starting point that can be implemented normally. MenuBarExtra lifecycle/composition stays in the app; services, state and reducers stay in Core.\\n\\n## Desktop distribution and app-only frameworks\\n\\nSet `macos.hardened_runtime: true` for Developer ID distribution. `macos.info_plist` adds string/bool host metadata (for example update-feed URLs and public signing keys); reserved identity keys remain owned by the normal project fields. Put a package on `target: \\\"app\\\"` when its framework belongs in the host UI/lifecycle rather than Core. App-only packages are excluded from the Core SwiftPM manifest and its unit tests. Omitting `target` keeps the existing Core behavior. Re-running the generator converges all these fields.\\n\\nFor Sparkle distribution use archive/export with the Developer ID method so nested helpers are signed, notarize and staple the app, then create/notarize/staple the DMG and generate the EdDSA-signed appcast. Never put API keys or private update signing keys in project JSON or manifests.\\n===GENERATOR-HELP===\\nManage iOS app project scaffolding\\n\\nUsage:\\n  ios-app-manager [command]\\n\\nAvailable Commands:\\n                       \\n  app-config           Manage AppConfig setup\\n  app-extensions       Manage app extension scaffolding\\n  app-intents          Manage App Intents scaffolding\\n  clean                Clean generated artifacts and caches\\n  completion           Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell\\n  dep                  Manage dependencies\\n  diagram              Generate PlantUML module dependency diagram\\n  entitlements         List entitlements from plist file\\n  fireauth-relux       Manage FireAuthRelux composition\\n  foundation-plus      Manage FoundationPlus module\\n  generate             Generate project artifacts\\n  help                 Help about any command\\n  http-client          Manage HttpClient IoC registration\\n  init                 Initialize a new project\\n  ioc                  Manage IoC container\\n  live-activity        Manage Live Activity scaffolding\\n  m                    Run mutation DSL\\n  module               Manage modules\\n  notification-service Manage Notification Service Extension scaffolding\\n  profile              Profile build, runtime, and rendered layout diagnostics\\n  push                 Push notification tools\\n  q                    Run query DSL\\n  relux                Manage Relux setup\\n  secure-store         Manage SecureStore module\\n  static-widget        Manage static widget scaffolding\\n  status               Show project status\\n  swiftui-plus         Manage SwiftUIPlus module\\n  test-targets         Manage test target scaffolding\\n  token-provider       Manage TokenProvider module\\n  utilities            Manage Utilities module\\n  widget-base          Manage WidgetKit base extension scaffolding\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -c, --config string   Path to project config JSON file (default \\\"ios-app-manager.json\\\")\\n  -h, --help            help for ios-app-manager\\n  -v, --verbose         Enable verbose output\\n      --version         version for ios-app-manager\\n\\nUse \\\"ios-app-manager [command] --help\\\" for more information about a command.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5468,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1367,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
